achability", "args": {"source": 45, "target": 1860, "window": [18031, 56431], "max_wait": 600}, "result_digest": "a832b4e61d90ed16", "result_summary": "{\"max_wait\": 600, \"n_nodes_reached\": 48, \"reached\": false, \"source\": 45, \"target\": 1860, \"window\": [18031, 56431]}", "latency_ms": 12, "tokens_before": 40831, "tokens_after": 40831, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_13", "tool": "edges_between", "args": {"u": 1006, "v": 45, "window": [18031, 56431]}, "result_digest": "a133e32997f8df86", "result_summary": "{\"connected\": true, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 1, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 0, \"u\": 1006, \"v\": 45, \"window\": [18031, 56431]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 40831, "tokens_after": 40831, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_68f9c03d", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1006, 1860], "window": [18031, 56431], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade from 1006 to 1860 within max_wait=600. Direct reachability fails (only 9 nodes reached) and path enumeration returns empty. A connection exists only when the wait constraint is removed, but that 9-hop route has gaps of 4961, 2873, 2104, 1930 and 9109 units \u2014 seven of eight hops violate the 600 bound \u2014 so it reflects static connectivity, not propagation. Alternative explanations are ruled out: the window is high-volume (6901 events) with popular hub intermediaries (153, 1680, 182) and bursty activity, yet still yields no valid chain; and the failure is not merely source sparsity, since even starting from hub 45 the target remains unreachable within 600. The out-neighbourhood of 1006 and in-neighbourhood of 1860 are disjoint. Result is robust to relaxing the threshold to 2000."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no genuine cascade.**\n\nKey findings:\n\n1. **Direct test fails** (step_01, step_09): under the 600-unit constraint, 1006 reaches only 9 nodes and 1860 is not among them; zero time-respecting paths enumerated.\n\n2. **The untimed/relaxed connection is a confounder** (step_03): a path *does* exist when the wait constraint is dropped \u2014 but its hop waits are 372, 4961, 217, 2873, 2104, 1930, 1025, **9109**. Seven of eight gaps exceed 600, some by 15\u00d7. This is a 9-hop chain stitched across ~22,600 time units of idling, not a propagating influence. Step_04 similarly confirms dense static 2-hop connectivity that dissolves under timing.\n\n3. **Volume/popularity are confounders, not evidence** (step_02, step_10, step_11): the window holds 6,901 events over 1,936 nodes, and the intermediaries include heavy hubs (153 with 162 events/134 partners; 1680 with 72; 182 with 68). Activity is bursty (bins of 1,460/1,622/1,416). Abundant traffic and popular brokers still fail to produce a valid chain.\n\n4. **Bottleneck localized** (step_12, step_13): 1006\u219245 fires exactly once. Even starting *from* hub 45 with a free choice of departure time, only 48 nodes are reachable within 600 and 1860 is still not one of them. So the failure is not 1006's sparsity (6 events, step_05) \u2014 the constraint breaks downstream, in the approach to 1860, whose in-neighbours (153, 182, 743, 958, 1390; step_08) are disjoint from 1006's out-neighbours (45, 230, 925, 1532, 1680; step_07).\n\n5. **Robustness**: raising the tolerance to 2000 units still fails, reaching only 14 nodes (step_06) \u2014 the negative is not knife-edge on the 600 threshold.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_68f9c03d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 1006 to 1860 within max_wait=600. Direct reachability fails (only 9 nodes reached) and path enumeration returns empty. A connection exists only when the wait constraint is removed, but that 9-hop route has gaps of 4961, 2873, 2104, 1930 and 9109 units \u2014 seven of eight hops violate the 600 bound \u2014 so it reflects static connectivity, not propagation. Alternative explanations are ruled out: the window is high-volume (6901 events) with popular hub intermediaries (153, 1680, 182) and bursty activity, yet still yields no valid chain; and the failure is not merely source sparsity, since even starting from hub 45 the target remains unreachable within 600. The out-neighbourhood of 1006 and in-neighbourhood of 1860 are disjoint. Result is robust to relaxing the threshold to 2000.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 50377, "total_output_tokens": 